Fixes "main.ERROR: Braintree\Configuration::merchantId needs to be set (or accessToken needs to be passed to Braintree\Gateway)."
being logged on every uncached product page render when Braintree is installed but not configured.

Root cause: braintree-core 4.8.0 added the Apple Pay product page button (block product.info.addtocart.applepayButton
in catalog_product_view.xml). Its constructor (Block\ApplePay\AbstractButton) calls Model\ApplePay\Auth::get(), which
generates a Braintree client token through ApplePay\Ui\ConfigProvider::getClientToken() before the block checks
whether Apple Pay is active. Without credentials the SDK throws and BraintreeAdapter::generate() logs the error.
The same token is generated for the anonymous GET /V1/applepay/auth endpoint.
Fix: getClientToken() returns null when Braintree Apple Pay is inactive, the same check getConfig() already does.

